      "widgets_values": [
        "AV EXTENSION\n\nUse H3 AV EXTENSION CONTROLLER to choose the start mode, number of active extensions, audio feather, previews, and Existing Video source-audio policy.\n\nExisting Video uses the normal VHS video loader so the loaded clip remains visible in its preview. Its VHS audio output is intentionally left unconnected. Keep source audio extracts the selected file safely inside H3; a video with no audio stream becomes exact-duration silence. Regenerate with H3 synthesizes a new soundtrack while protecting the complete source picture.\n\nT2V generates a starter without an image keyframe. I2V / Custom Keyframes enables the starter image/keyframe group.\n\nSet prompts/references in the active generation groups. Reference Audio 1 and 2 are optional and bypassed by default. The controller enables/bypasses managed extension groups from Active Extensions.\n\nUPDATE 9\nInput video must be constant 24 fps. Keep source audio protects the context; only its final 8 audio ticks (0.2 s) gradually receive denoising. The entire 39-frame context is NOT regenerated. Final overlap uses the extension decode, so VAE reconstruction can still differ slightly. Output prefix supports %date:yyyy-MM-dd%/MiniMax_H3_ (server local date)."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "AV EXTENSION\n\nUse H3 AV EXTENSION CONTROLLER to choose the start mode, number of active extensions, audio feather, previews, and Existing Video source-audio policy.\n\nExisting Video uses the normal VHS video loader so the loaded clip remains visible in its preview. Its VHS audio output is intentionally left unconnected. Keep source audio extracts the selected file safely inside H3; a video with no audio stream becomes exact-duration silence. Regenerate with H3 synthesizes a new soundtrack while protecting the complete source picture.\n\nT2V generates a starter without an image keyframe. I2V / Custom Keyframes enables the starter image/keyframe group.\n\nSet prompts/references in the active generation groups. Reference Audio 1 and 2 are optional and bypassed by default. The controller enables/bypasses managed extension groups from Active Extensions."
      },
